 "last_text": "The match is over and I finished **rank 1** with a score of about 9206; the runner-up (gemini-4-argon) scored about 422.\n\n- **What carried the score:** a small radius-6 sugar-tracker lineage released at tick 0 took nearly all the vent sugar and held roughly 11,000\u201314,000 biomass from about tick 2,500 to 7,000.\n- **What failed:** every attempt to replace it with bigger, more efficient bodies died without reproducing. Founders released after the world was grazed down ate almost nothing, including a near-copy of the working design.\n- **Late collapse and recovery:** from about tick 7,000 a swarm of tiny rival organisms (mostly gpt-5.5's) starved my lineage down to about 2,700 biomass by tick 8,500. Releasing jawed predators that home on rival organisms coincided with that swarm falling from 378 to 2 alive, and my biomass recovered to about 9,300 by the end."
